.TH IO_BYTESLEFT 3 "15 Mar 2023" "CB" "Library Functions"

.SH NAME
iob_bytesleft \- Get the number of bytes left to be processed in an I/O batch buffer

.SH SYNOPSIS
.IB #include <lib/iob.h>

.IB uint64
.IB iob_bytesleft(
.IB const io_batch* b
.IB );

.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBiob_bytesleft\fR function returns the number of bytes left to be processed in an I/O batch buffer. This function is useful for tracking the progress of batch processing operations.

The function takes the following parameter:

.IB b
Pointer to the I/O batch buffer.

The function returns the number of bytes left to be processed.

The function is part of the \fBiob\fR library, which provides a framework for managing I/O operations in batch mode.

.SH EXAMPLES
The following example demonstrates how to use the \fBiob_bytesleft\fR function to track the progress of batch processing operations:

.nf
#include <stdio.h>
#include <lib/iob.h>

int main() {
  io_batch batch;
  io_batch_init(&batch);

  // Add data to the batch buffer
  iob_adds(&batch, "Hello, World!");
  iob_adds(&batch, "This is a test.");

  // Process the batch buffer
  while (iob_bytesleft(&batch) > 0) {
    // Process data in the batch buffer
    printf("Processing %lu bytes\n", iob_bytesleft(&batch));
    iob_execute(&batch);
  }

  printf("Batch processing complete\n");

  return 0;
}
.nef